  "need": "Hazard: a Vietnamese lexical false positive. 'Mày râu' reads literally as eyebrows and beard, and a body-part query retrieves it as such; in the verse it is the whole of a man's grooming and, by extension, the man himself, and the couplet is a portrait of the buyer Mã Giám Sinh, not a description of facial hair. 'Trạc ngoại tứ tuần' compounds it: 'tuần' is a ten-day period elsewhere in the language and a decade of age here, so a reader who resolves the words one by one gets forty days rather than forty years.",
